#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119889 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119709 :question/id #uuid "4b202b4e-d8dc-524c-8cb4-ab0c00eb78cb" :question/math-academy-id "e-8958" :question/problem "![](images/95/95e3f2da04e23c9b42ea04cba3ee1d7cc069fef992592f09a70cef367b670f0d.png)\n\nThe integral above gives the surface area of the parametric surface $\\mathbf{r}(u,v) = \\big\\langle u, \\: v, \\: u^3-v \\big\\rangle$ for $0 \\leq u \\leq 3$ and $0 \\leq v \\leq 2.$ What is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf r (u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_S \\,\\textrm d S = \\iint\\limits_D  \\left\\|  \\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v \\right\\|  \\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{3}-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,3{u}^{2}⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{3}-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3{u}^{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3{u}^{2} \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3{u}^{2} \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3{u}^{2},\\,1,\\,1⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand its magnitude is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨-3{u}^{2},\\,1,\\,1⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(3{u}^{2})^{2}+(1)^{2}+(1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9{u}^{4}+2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{9{u}^{4}+2}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2928b0de-fadb-5ffa-b30f-72c0051f0ac6" :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558994 :question-generator/id #uuid "07e761a3-b1f5-5c61-8c49-dfcd9841b9e9" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186119889.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120073 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "054fe519-ab8b-5f85-ab9a-d3d159cab8ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}u\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡v+8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238123} {:answer/id #uuid "79000f71-931f-5f6e-9579-ea3d7e92e42d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+36}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239098} {:answer/id #uuid "ae4d4cc8-79ec-5532-8e6c-1a5240849a2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\sqrt{{u}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡v+{u}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239569} {:answer/id #uuid "ee50303c-a270-5c12-a05d-7f037348e740" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240154} {:answer/id #uuid "f622f3d7-b438-53d7-9272-6937b0c0643b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3{u}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡v+4{u}^{2}+36}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240225}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "054fe519-ab8b-5f85-ab9a-d3d159cab8ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}u\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡v+8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238123} :answer-field/id #uuid "f15110c7-0c2f-5ea3-8cdf-522b5ef09c66" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240754}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d4d337cb-e76c-55f1-8712-82ae25a0b484" :question/math-academy-id "q-105613" :question/problem "$$\n{∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A,\\,D={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le \\pi }\n$$\n\nThe integral above gives the surface area of the parametric surface $r(u,v)=⟨2u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,3u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,u⟩$ for $0\\le u\\le 1$ and $0\\le v\\le \\pi .$ What is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(3u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(3u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,-3u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡v & 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡v & 1 \\\\ 2u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v & -3u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡v & 1 \\\\ -3u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡v & 1 \\\\ 2u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡v & 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡v \\\\ 2u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v & -3u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,2u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,-6u{sin}^{2}⁡v-6u{cos}^{2}⁡v⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,2u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,-6u⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨3u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,2u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,-6u⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(3u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v)^{2}+(2u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v)^{2}+(-6u)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9{u}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡v+4{u}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡v+36{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(5{u}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡v+4{u}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡v)+4{u}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡v+36{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5{u}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡v+4{u}^{2}({sin}^{2}⁡v+{cos}^{2}⁡v)+36{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5{u}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡v+4{u}^{2}+36{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5{u}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡v+40{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5{u}^{2}({sin}^{2}⁡v+8)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5{u}^{2}}\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡v+8} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}u\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡v+8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $\\sqrt{{u}^{2}}=u$ since $u\\ge 0$ on $D.$\n\nTherefore, the surface area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{5}u\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡v+8}\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120091 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "319007b2-b622-521a-9fbd-6b55411ba8fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2v\\sqrt{1+8{u}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244758} {:answer/id #uuid "77d27a23-474c-5fd8-b89a-b5cf94e06791" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u\\sqrt{1+4v}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245376} {:answer/id #uuid "93b89d68-2ae3-5725-a00d-dea53dab7aaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{{v}^{2}-{u}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245602} {:answer/id #uuid "a4251703-6830-575d-b816-b1664fbed324" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+{v}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245780} {:answer/id #uuid "ffcccb75-fd9a-544a-9328-801afbd6a123" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{v}^{2}\\sqrt{1+4{u}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246547}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "319007b2-b622-521a-9fbd-6b55411ba8fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2v\\sqrt{1+8{u}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244758} :answer-field/id #uuid "8bbe3440-ff66-5a42-bcf4-05a3f9473d00" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246790}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a126827b-bc56-516e-a030-80e53d51bfcf" :question/math-academy-id "q-109941" :question/problem "$$\n{∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A,\\,D={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 2,\\,0\\le v\\le 2}\n$$\n\nThe integral above gives the surface area of the parametric surface $r(u,v)=⟨{u}^{2},\\,u-{v}^{2},\\,{v}^{2}⟩$ for $0\\le u\\le 2$ and $0\\le v\\le 2.$ What is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u-{v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({v}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2u,\\,1,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u-{v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({v}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,-2v,\\,2v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2u & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2v & 2v\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2v & 2v\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}2u & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2v\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2u & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2v\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2v,\\,-4uv,\\,-4uv⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨2v,\\,-4uv,\\,-4uv⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2v)^{2}+(-4uv)^{2}+(-4uv)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{v}^{2}+16{u}^{2}{v}^{2}+16{u}^{2}{v}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{v}^{2}+32{u}^{2}{v}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{v}^{2}(1+8{u}^{2})} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{v}^{2}}\\sqrt{1+8{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =2v\\sqrt{1+8{u}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $\\sqrt{{v}^{2}}=v$ since $v\\ge 0$ on $D.$\n\nTherefore, the surface area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2v\\sqrt{1+8{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247065 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5e41b296-1fe0-5842-854b-f480f12525fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{u}\\sqrt{u+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245145} {:answer/id #uuid "87cd26ad-a962-56ea-bdee-5e602d62af6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2u}\\sqrt{\\operatorname{cos}⁡v+\\operatorname{sin}⁡v}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245510} {:answer/id #uuid "97c12a1b-9a2b-5781-8bcb-d79f575b9c1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{u}\\sqrt{{e}^{2u}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245655} {:answer/id #uuid "a1a80cc0-881d-5ed4-b72e-87eb79fb4fc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{u}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v\\operatorname{sin}⁡v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245752} {:answer/id #uuid "a67a985a-4d91-553c-91f4-71e58ab8a6af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{{e}^{u}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v\\operatorname{sin}⁡v}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245803}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "97c12a1b-9a2b-5781-8bcb-d79f575b9c1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{u}\\sqrt{{e}^{2u}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245655} :answer-field/id #uuid "31c52917-76e8-5845-8126-fd7d10803407" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246628}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3edff3d6-2a79-51e6-bf36-1af5081d0991" :question/math-academy-id "q-109948" :question/problem "$$\n{∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A,\\,D={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 4,\\,0\\le v\\le \\pi }\n$$\n\nThe integral above gives the surface area of the parametric surface $r(u,v)=⟨u,\\,{e}^{u}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,{e}^{u}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v⟩$ for $0\\le u\\le 4$ and $0\\le v\\le \\pi .$ What is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({e}^{u}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({e}^{u}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,{e}^{u}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,{e}^{u}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({e}^{u}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({e}^{u}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,{e}^{u}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,-{e}^{u}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & {e}^{u}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v & {e}^{u}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v \\\\ 0 & {e}^{u}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v & -{e}^{u}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}{e}^{u}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v & {e}^{u}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v \\\\ {e}^{u}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v & -{e}^{u}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & {e}^{u}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v \\\\ 0 & -{e}^{u}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & {e}^{u}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\ 0 & {e}^{u}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-{e}^{2u}({sin}^{2}⁡v+{cos}^{2}⁡v),\\,{e}^{u}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,{e}^{u}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-{e}^{2u},\\,{e}^{u}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,{e}^{u}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨-{e}^{2u},\\,{e}^{u}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,{e}^{u}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-{e}^{2u})^{2}+({e}^{u}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v)^{2}+({e}^{u}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{e}^{4u}+{e}^{2u}{sin}^{2}⁡v+{e}^{2u}{cos}^{2}⁡v} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{e}^{4u}+{e}^{2u}({sin}^{2}⁡v+{cos}^{2}⁡v)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{e}^{4u}+{e}^{2u}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{e}^{2u}({e}^{2u}+1)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{e}^{2u}}\\sqrt{{e}^{2u}+1} \\\\  & ={e}^{u}\\sqrt{{e}^{2u}+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}{e}^{u}\\sqrt{{e}^{2u}+1}\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247071 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0aba1084-dd62-5f6d-8414-67325a66d2b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+{cos}^{2}⁡v}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244408} {:answer/id #uuid "3262fefb-ad44-55d0-9d7c-75f64ce5ef28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{1+2{u}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244764} {:answer/id #uuid "4c7dc017-c361-5e32-9ac8-b550df86db3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2u\\sqrt{1+{u}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡v}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244996} {:answer/id #uuid "a6b7b5f0-4589-56a5-a613-5fdf9f4f5425" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡v\\sqrt{1+{u}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245804} {:answer/id #uuid "c2a8dda4-db10-5e30-883a-9f6d8c1666a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2u\\sqrt{1+{u}^{2}+3{u}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡v}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246050}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c2a8dda4-db10-5e30-883a-9f6d8c1666a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2u\\sqrt{1+{u}^{2}+3{u}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡v}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246050} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e682a7f-849f-592f-9a4e-0dc921cdf99a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246823}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ae0a4a11-25db-5593-ba23-9a81fd0d6c49" :question/math-academy-id "q-110019" :question/problem "$$\n{∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A,\\,D={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 2,\\,0\\le v\\le \\pi }\n$$\n\nThe integral above gives the surface area of the parametric surface $r(u,v)=⟨{u}^{2},\\,2u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v⟩$ for $0\\le u\\le 1$ and $0\\le v\\le \\pi .$ What is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2u,\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡v⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,-u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2u & 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡v & \\operatorname{cos}⁡v \\\\ 0 & 2u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v & -u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡v & \\operatorname{cos}⁡v \\\\ 2u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v & -u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}2u & \\operatorname{cos}⁡v \\\\ 0 & -u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2u & 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\ 0 & 2u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2u{sin}^{2}⁡v-2u{cos}^{2}⁡v,\\,2{u}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,4{u}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2u,\\,2{u}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,4{u}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨-2u,\\,2{u}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,4{u}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2u)^{2}+(2{u}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v)^{2}+(4{u}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{u}^{2}+4{u}^{4}{sin}^{2}⁡v+16{u}^{4}{cos}^{2}⁡v} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{u}^{2}+4{u}^{4}({sin}^{2}⁡v+{cos}^{2}⁡v)+12{u}^{4}{cos}^{2}⁡v} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{u}^{2}+4{u}^{4}+12{u}^{4}{cos}^{2}⁡v} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{u}^{2}(1+{u}^{2}+3{u}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡v)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{u}^{2}}\\sqrt{1+{u}^{2}+3{u}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡v} \\\\  & =2u\\sqrt{1+{u}^{2}+3{u}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡v}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $\\sqrt{{u}^{2}}=u$ since $u\\ge 0$ on $D.$\n\nTherefore, the surface area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2u\\sqrt{1+{u}^{2}+3{u}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡v}\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186397957 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e335f1ce-f85b-55fb-9898-0984e81e5a0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397959} {:answer/id #uuid "058877bc-b659-5e3e-87cf-faeec5fcf705" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397960} {:answer/id #uuid "cd8caafa-3ec3-522c-ad87-8c146d142f74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u\\sqrt{{v}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397961} {:answer/id #uuid "354ff6f5-50a5-5ef5-9619-794c2e23d89b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{u+v}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397962} {:answer/id #uuid "a8e0a436-d109-5391-b4da-ce44a96c863e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397963}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a8e0a436-d109-5391-b4da-ce44a96c863e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397963} :answer-field/id #uuid "3dc7b100-8716-5ef0-ac33-e0d012d77654" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397958}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8259cc12-8425-5d9e-923a-3106edaae5d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-109943" :question/problem "$$\n{∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A,\\,D={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 2}\n$$\n\nThe integral above gives the surface area of the parametric surface $r(u,v)=⟨u+v,\\,3-v,\\,1+4u+5v⟩$ for $0\\le u\\le 1$ and $0\\le v\\le 2.$ What is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(3-v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(1+4u+5v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,4⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(3-v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(1+4u+5v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-1,\\,5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 5\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,\\,-1,\\,-1⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨4,\\,-1,\\,-1⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(4)^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+1+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{18} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}3\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186397964 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5545b0b7-751d-5798-9bd4-dfa8faf23f03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397966} {:answer/id #uuid "a470c598-2c0a-5ceb-ac0e-1fb73e235141" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2u\\sqrt{9{u}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397967} {:answer/id #uuid "dade9321-241a-5817-902c-2195520cffda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397968} {:answer/id #uuid "2e7e02df-d389-5236-a15d-ad10a54c5136" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{18{u}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397969} {:answer/id #uuid "c8a959ef-e722-5be5-9bcf-f1870eca1b7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397970}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e7e02df-d389-5236-a15d-ad10a54c5136" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{18{u}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397969} :answer-field/id #uuid "96083256-eb07-5ebd-a86e-e5865f463363" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397965}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c235bda4-b647-59f5-b137-7fc5bc86576a" :question/math-academy-id "q-109947" :question/problem "$$\n{∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A,\\,D={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 1}\n$$\n\nThe integral above gives the surface area of the parametric surface $r(u,v)=⟨u+v,\\,3{u}^{2},\\,u-v⟩$ for $0\\le u\\le 1$ and $0\\le v\\le 1.$ What is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(3{u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,6u,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(3{u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 6u & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}6u & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 6u \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-6u,\\,2,\\,-6u⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨-6u,\\,2,\\,-6u⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-6u)^{2}+(2)^{2}+(-6u)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36{u}^{2}+4+36{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{72{u}^{2}+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4(18{u}^{2}+1)} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{18{u}^{2}+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2\\sqrt{18{u}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186397971 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a16278f-a652-5ce3-b9f8-9f80d8b88232" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+{v}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397973} {:answer/id #uuid "8a1a6ff8-553d-5774-99ac-38531f54fba5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{{u}^{4}+{v}^{4}+4{u}^{2}{v}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397974} {:answer/id #uuid "a0d50f4f-f2ad-5974-83b1-c8764b04094b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{u}^{2}v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397975} {:answer/id #uuid "c4340729-f530-5302-81b0-b5b30177bfba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397976} {:answer/id #uuid "21efbbd9-845c-5789-8305-5927df10c402" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2u\\sqrt{{v}^{2}+uv}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397977}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8a1a6ff8-553d-5774-99ac-38531f54fba5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{{u}^{4}+{v}^{4}+4{u}^{2}{v}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397974} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b095c98-f0c4-52f0-b54c-c5176a3e6c0c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397972}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0aca92da-c648-5c8b-ae46-3b81f8b99c27" :question/math-academy-id "q-109951" :question/problem "$$\n{∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A,\\,D={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 2,\\,0\\le v\\le 4}\n$$\n\nThe integral above gives the surface area of the parametric surface $r(u,v)=⟨{u}^{2},\\,{v}^{2},\\,uv⟩$ for $0\\le u\\le 2$ and $0\\le v\\le 4.$ What is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(uv)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2u,\\,0,\\,v⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(uv)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2v,\\,u⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2u & 0 & v \\\\ 0 & 2v & u\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & v \\\\ 2v & u\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}2u & v \\\\ 0 & u\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2u & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2v\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2{v}^{2},\\,-2{u}^{2},\\,4uv⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨-2{v}^{2},\\,-2{u}^{2},\\,4uv⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-2{v}^{2})^{2}+(-2{u}^{2})^{2}+(4uv)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{v}^{4}+4{u}^{4}+16{u}^{2}{v}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4({u}^{4}+{v}^{4}+4{u}^{2}{v}^{2})} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{{u}^{4}+{v}^{4}+4{u}^{2}{v}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2\\sqrt{{u}^{4}+{v}^{4}+4{u}^{2}{v}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558981 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "011655a2-c520-5cd0-a439-defc348c17b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558974} {:answer/id #uuid "48815a36-e11f-5e50-85f2-1df30f980d9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558980} {:answer/id #uuid "91e08695-6405-567c-8d4e-0b8f3347a5f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\sqrt{u + v}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558986} {:answer/id #uuid "a0bde4ca-48f5-5c86-ad8e-88083b8a8731" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{14}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558987} {:answer/id #uuid "ed23ef92-0aad-5b95-947e-ba7002f159c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u \\sqrt{v^{2} + 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558992}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a0bde4ca-48f5-5c86-ad8e-88083b8a8731" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{14}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558987} :answer-field/id #uuid "32a31c4b-f831-5da9-8f29-1b931744a7c9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558977}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6ce03692-58d4-5830-8d97-d77704c638fb" :question/problem "$$\n\\iint_D\\boxed{}\\,\\mathrm{d}A,\\quad D=\\{(u,v):0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 2\\}\n$$\n\nThe integral above gives the surface area of the parametric surface $r(u,v)=\\langle u + v,\\,3 - v,\\,3 u + 5 v + 1\\rangle$ for $0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 2.$ What is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\iint_S\\mathrm{d}S=\\iint_D\\left\\|\\mathbf r_u\\times\\mathbf r_v\\right\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf r_u &=\\langle \\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial u},\\,\\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial u},\\,\\frac{\\partial z}{\\partial u}\\rangle \\\\  &=\\langle \\frac{\\partial}{\\partial u}\\left(u + v\\right),\\,\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial u}\\left(3 - v\\right),\\,\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial u}\\left(3 u + 5 v + 1\\right)\\rangle \\\\  &=\\langle 1,\\,0,\\,3\\rangle \\\\ \\mathbf r_v &=\\langle \\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial v},\\,\\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial v},\\,\\frac{\\partial z}{\\partial v}\\rangle \\\\  &=\\langle \\frac{\\partial}{\\partial v}\\left(u + v\\right),\\,\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial v}\\left(3 - v\\right),\\,\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial v}\\left(3 u + 5 v + 1\\right)\\rangle \\\\  &=\\langle 1,\\,-1,\\,5\\rangle\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf r_u\\times\\mathbf r_v &=\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 5\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  &=\\langle \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 5\\end{vmatrix},\\,-\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{vmatrix},\\,\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{vmatrix}\\rangle \\\\  &=\\langle 3,\\,-2,\\,-1\\rangle\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\|\\mathbf r_u\\times\\mathbf r_v\\right\\| &=\\left\\|\\langle 3,\\,-2,\\,-1\\rangle\\right\\| \\\\  &=\\sqrt{\\left(3\\right)^2+\\left(-2\\right)^2+\\left(-1\\right)^2} \\\\  &=\\sqrt{9+4+1} \\\\  &=\\sqrt{14} \\\\  &=\\sqrt{14}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\iint_S\\mathrm{d}S &=\\iint_D\\left\\|\\mathbf r_u\\times\\mathbf r_v\\right\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}A \\\\  &=\\iint_D \\sqrt{14}\\,\\mathrm{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558989 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b115ea7-8c75-582e-bcb9-c63407864ed8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u \\sqrt{16 v + 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558975} {:answer/id #uuid "3bbc89bf-4b41-500d-a74f-a5a23cc77a9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{4 u^{2} + v^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558978} {:answer/id #uuid "43feaff8-ab49-5cc0-a22e-c79061a43457" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 v \\sqrt{32 u^{2} + 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558979} {:answer/id #uuid "733b93c8-4090-5697-9f6e-1b3b25a0447f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{- 4 u^{2} + v^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558984} {:answer/id #uuid "a2f43bf4-274b-5f91-890a-212b06e6e8c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "v^{2} \\sqrt{16 u^{2} + 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558988}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "43feaff8-ab49-5cc0-a22e-c79061a43457" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 v \\sqrt{32 u^{2} + 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558979} :answer-field/id #uuid "8cf6d408-766c-507b-a6fd-42b33e06fe2a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558985}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c17b6edc-1f0e-51cb-a0ce-11f93aba061f" :question/problem "$$\n\\iint_D\\boxed{}\\,\\mathrm{d}A,\\quad D=\\{(u,v):0\\le u\\le 2,\\,0\\le v\\le 2\\}\n$$\n\nThe integral above gives the surface area of the parametric surface $r(u,v)=\\langle 2 u^{2},\\,u - v^{2},\\,v^{2}\\rangle$ for $0\\le u\\le 2,\\,0\\le v\\le 2.$ What is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\iint_S\\mathrm{d}S=\\iint_D\\left\\|\\mathbf r_u\\times\\mathbf r_v\\right\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf r_u &=\\langle \\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial u},\\,\\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial u},\\,\\frac{\\partial z}{\\partial u}\\rangle \\\\  &=\\langle \\frac{\\partial}{\\partial u}\\left(2 u^{2}\\right),\\,\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial u}\\left(u - v^{2}\\right),\\,\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial u}\\left(v^{2}\\right)\\rangle \\\\  &=\\langle 4 u,\\,1,\\,0\\rangle \\\\ \\mathbf r_v &=\\langle \\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial v},\\,\\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial v},\\,\\frac{\\partial z}{\\partial v}\\rangle \\\\  &=\\langle \\frac{\\partial}{\\partial v}\\left(2 u^{2}\\right),\\,\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial v}\\left(u - v^{2}\\right),\\,\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial v}\\left(v^{2}\\right)\\rangle \\\\  &=\\langle 0,\\,- 2 v,\\,2 v\\rangle\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf r_u\\times\\mathbf r_v &=\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 4 u & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & - 2 v & 2 v\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  &=\\langle \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ - 2 v & 2 v\\end{vmatrix},\\,-\\begin{vmatrix}4 u & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 v\\end{vmatrix},\\,\\begin{vmatrix}4 u & 1 \\\\ 0 & - 2 v\\end{vmatrix}\\rangle \\\\  &=\\langle 2 v,\\,- 8 u v,\\,- 8 u v\\rangle\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\|\\mathbf r_u\\times\\mathbf r_v\\right\\| &=\\left\\|\\langle 2 v,\\,- 8 u v,\\,- 8 u v\\rangle\\right\\| \\\\  &=\\sqrt{\\left(2 v\\right)^2+\\left(- 8 u v\\right)^2+\\left(- 8 u v\\right)^2} \\\\  &=\\sqrt{4 v^{2}+64 u^{2} v^{2}+64 u^{2} v^{2}} \\\\  &=\\sqrt{128 u^{2} v^{2} + 4 v^{2}} \\\\  &=\\sqrt{4 v^{2} \\left(32 u^{2} + 1\\right)} \\\\  &=\\sqrt{4 v^{2}}\\sqrt{32 u^{2} + 1} \\\\  &=2 v \\sqrt{32 u^{2} + 1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $\\sqrt{v^2}=v$ since $v\\ge 0$ on $D.$\n\nTherefore, the surface area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\iint_S\\mathrm{d}S &=\\iint_D\\left\\|\\mathbf r_u\\times\\mathbf r_v\\right\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}A \\\\  &=\\iint_D 2 v \\sqrt{32 u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186558993 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00cee569-5cea-5d57-9bc3-3903a71989af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558973} {:answer/id #uuid "0f83c76d-ec99-5241-aebf-9c4270e1a7ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u \\sqrt{v^{2} + 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558976} {:answer/id #uuid "6ce6fda6-b951-5d87-8a85-6283f433ac85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\sqrt{u + v}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558982} {:answer/id #uuid "cd1295a6-0f95-51f3-8fd1-ee96277ead12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558990} {:answer/id #uuid "d2a1a18a-411a-5224-a056-02a4076cbe0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{30}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558991}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d2a1a18a-411a-5224-a056-02a4076cbe0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{30}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558991} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ffdcbfe-e3c8-554c-90ac-7c7fa5fdd703" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558983}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f12a3689-dba6-56d9-843d-c0f7bf0ac72a" :question/problem "$$\n\\iint_D\\boxed{}\\,\\mathrm{d}A,\\quad D=\\{(u,v):0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 2\\}\n$$\n\nThe integral above gives the surface area of the parametric surface $r(u,v)=\\langle u + v,\\,3 - v,\\,5 u + 7 v + 1\\rangle$ for $0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 2.$ What is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\iint_S\\mathrm{d}S=\\iint_D\\left\\|\\mathbf r_u\\times\\mathbf r_v\\right\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf r_u &=\\langle \\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial u},\\,\\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial u},\\,\\frac{\\partial z}{\\partial u}\\rangle \\\\  &=\\langle \\frac{\\partial}{\\partial u}\\left(u + v\\right),\\,\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial u}\\left(3 - v\\right),\\,\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial u}\\left(5 u + 7 v + 1\\right)\\rangle \\\\  &=\\langle 1,\\,0,\\,5\\rangle \\\\ \\mathbf r_v &=\\langle \\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial v},\\,\\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial v},\\,\\frac{\\partial z}{\\partial v}\\rangle \\\\  &=\\langle \\frac{\\partial}{\\partial v}\\left(u + v\\right),\\,\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial v}\\left(3 - v\\right),\\,\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial v}\\left(5 u + 7 v + 1\\right)\\rangle \\\\  &=\\langle 1,\\,-1,\\,7\\rangle\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf r_u\\times\\mathbf r_v &=\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 7\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  &=\\langle \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 7\\end{vmatrix},\\,-\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 7\\end{vmatrix},\\,\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{vmatrix}\\rangle \\\\  &=\\langle 5,\\,-2,\\,-1\\rangle\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\|\\mathbf r_u\\times\\mathbf r_v\\right\\| &=\\left\\|\\langle 5,\\,-2,\\,-1\\rangle\\right\\| \\\\  &=\\sqrt{\\left(5\\right)^2+\\left(-2\\right)^2+\\left(-1\\right)^2} \\\\  &=\\sqrt{25+4+1} \\\\  &=\\sqrt{30} \\\\  &=\\sqrt{30}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\iint_S\\mathrm{d}S &=\\iint_D\\left\\|\\mathbf r_u\\times\\mathbf r_v\\right\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}A \\\\  &=\\iint_D \\sqrt{30}\\,\\mathrm{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Integral That Represents the Surface Area of a Parametric Surface"}]}
